<title>USA: US Treasury 5-year notes seen yielding 6.76 pct.</title>
<headline>US Treasury 5-year notes seen yielding 6.76 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury's auction of $12.5 billion in five-year notes on Wednesday should produce a yield near 6.76 percent, dealers said.</p>
<p>Shortly before the bidding deadline of 1300 EDT/1700 GMT, the five-year notes were trading with a when-issued yield of 6.755 percent.</p>
<p>Results for the auction are expected around 1345 EDT/1745 GMT.</p>
<p>(( -- North American Treasury Desk, 212-859-1679 ))</p>
